# Nexus v2.0 — Task Breakdown

## Phase 1: Foundation Layer

### P1.1 — Theme System
- [x] T1.1.1: Create `internal/theme/theme.go` with Theme struct (semantic color map: bg, fg, accent, error, warning, success, info, subtle, highlight, cursor, selection, border, header, muted + mode colors + protocol colors + status colors)
- [ ] T1.1.2: Implement TokyoNight Storm theme as default
- [ ] T1.1.3: Implement built-in themes: catppuccin-mocha, dracula, gruvbox-dark, nord
- [ ] T1.1.4: Add YAML skin file loader (`~/.config/nexus/theme.yaml`)
- [ ] T1.1.5: Create `internal/theme/styles.go` — lipgloss style factory that generates all app styles from a Theme
- [ ] T1.1.6: Refactor `internal/tui/styles.go` to use theme system (remove hardcoded colors)
- [ ] T1.1.7: Add `:theme` command to switch themes at runtime
- [ ] T1.1.8: Unit tests for theme loading and style generation

### P1.2 — Modal System
- [ ] T1.2.1: Create `internal/tui/mode.go` with Mode type (Normal, Insert, Visual, Command) and state machine
- [ ] T1.2.2: Add ModeChangedMsg and mode field to App struct
- [ ] T1.2.3: Route key events through mode dispatcher in App.Update()
- [ ] T1.2.4: Normal mode: all current keybindings work as-is
- [ ] T1.2.5: Insert mode: only active in text input contexts (filter, command, form), forward keys to input
- [ ] T1.2.6: Visual mode: multi-select state, toggle with v/V, track selection set
- [ ] T1.2.7: Command mode: `:` and `/` and `?` entry, Esc exits
- [ ] T1.2.8: Esc always returns to Normal from any mode
- [ ] T1.2.9: Mode indicator in statusbar with color per mode (NORMAL=blue, INSERT=green, VISUAL=purple, COMMAND=yellow)
- [ ] T1.2.10: Unit tests for mode transitions

### P1.3 — Vim Motion Engine
- [ ] T1.3.1: Create `internal/tui/motion.go` with MotionEngine struct
- [ ] T1.3.2: Count accumulator: digit keys (1-9) build count prefix, reset on non-digit or action
- [ ] T1.3.3: Motion types: j/k (line), gg/G (absolute), Ctrl+d/u (half-page), Ctrl+f/b (full-page), H/M/L (screen)
- [ ] T1.3.4: Operator pending state: d/y/c set pending operator, next motion applies it
- [ ] T1.3.5: Doubled operators: dd (delete current), yy (yank current), cc (change current)
- [ ] T1.3.6: Operator + motion: dG (delete to end), dgg (delete to start), d5j (delete 5 down)
- [ ] T1.3.7: Count + motion: 5j (move 5 down), 10G (go to item 10)
- [ ] T1.3.8: Integration with App.Update() — motion results applied to table/list cursor
- [ ] T1.3.9: Table-driven unit tests for all motion/operator combinations

### P1.4 — k9s-Style Table
- [ ] T1.4.1: Create `internal/tui/table.go` with custom Table model (replace bubbles/table)
- [ ] T1.4.2: Column definition: name, width (min/max/flex), alignment, sort key
- [ ] T1.4.3: Column headers with sort indicators (▲ ascending, ▼ descending)
- [ ] T1.4.4: Sort by column: Shift+N (name), Shift+H (host), Shift+S (status), Shift+P (protocol), Shift+G (group)
- [ ] T1.4.5: Row rendering with cursor bar highlight (full-width background color)
- [ ] T1.4.6: Row striping (alternating subtle background)
- [ ] T1.4.7: Status column: colored indicators (● green online, ○ red offline, ◐ yellow degraded, ? grey unknown)
- [ ] T1.4.8: Latency column: color gradient (green <100ms, yellow <500ms, red >500ms)
- [ ] T1.4.9: Age column: human-readable duration formatting (2d3h, 15m, 3s)
- [ ] T1.4.10: Wide mode toggle (Ctrl+W): show/hide additional columns (port, username, tags, identity_file)
- [ ] T1.4.11: Column auto-sizing with minimum widths and flex allocation
- [ ] T1.4.12: Integration with motion engine (count+j/k, gg, G, H/M/L, Ctrl+d/u, Ctrl+f/b)
- [ ] T1.4.13: Migrate list.go to use new table (preserve all existing functionality)

### P1.5 — k9s-Style Layout Overhaul
- [ ] T1.5.1: Redesign header.go: logo left (NEXUS cyan), config file path right, k9s-style hotkey bar
- [ ] T1.5.2: Add title bar: current view name (bold) + item count + active filter indicator
- [ ] T1.5.3: Redesign statusbar.go: [MODE] left | connection stats center | flash | position (N/M) right
- [ ] T1.5.4: Move command/filter input to absolute bottom (below statusbar)
- [ ] T1.5.5: Crumbs bar: show navigation path (Connections > Production > detail)
- [ ] T1.5.6: Recalculate contentHeight() for new layout regions
- [ ] T1.5.7: Full layout render test at 80x24 minimum

## Phase 2: Core Interaction

### P2.1 — Leader Key + Which-Key
- [ ] T2.1.1: Create `internal/tui/leader.go` — leader key state machine
- [ ] T2.1.2: Space key enters leader-pending state, starts 500ms timer
