- [ ] T2.1.4: Which-key layout: grid of key-description pairs, grouped by category
- [ ] T2.1.5: Implement all leader key groups (c, f, s, g, i, e, t, v, h, p, o, ?)
- [ ] T2.1.6: Nested navigation: group key updates popup to sub-group
- [ ] T2.1.7: Dismiss on Esc, valid action key, or any non-matching key
- [ ] T2.1.8: Wire leader actions to existing and new functionality

### P2.2 — Incremental Search
- [ ] T2.2.1: Create `internal/tui/search.go` — search state machine
- [ ] T2.2.2: `/` forward search, `?` reverse search entry
- [ ] T2.2.3: Incremental filtering: live update table as user types
- [ ] T2.2.4: Search highlighting: matched text rendered with highlight style in table cells
- [ ] T2.2.5: Filter modes: regex, inverse (!), fuzzy (-f), tag (-t), group (-g)
- [ ] T2.2.6: n/N cycle through matches (move cursor to next/previous match)
- [ ] T2.2.7: * search for connection name under cursor, # reverse
- [ ] T2.2.8: Search history with up/down arrows
- [ ] T2.2.9: Active filter bar showing current filter with Esc to clear

### P2.3 — Visual Mode
- [ ] T2.3.1: Create `internal/tui/visual.go` — visual selection state
- [ ] T2.3.2: V enters line-visual (range selection with j/k extending)
- [ ] T2.3.3: v toggles selection on current item (non-contiguous multi-select)
- [ ] T2.3.4: Render selected rows with selection highlight style
- [ ] T2.3.5: Selected count in statusbar: "-- VISUAL (3 selected) --"
- [ ] T2.3.6: d operator on selection: delete all selected (with confirmation)
- [ ] T2.3.7: y operator on selection: yank all selected to clipboard
- [ ] T2.3.8: Tag operations on selection: `:tag add production` applies to selected
- [ ] T2.3.9: Esc exits visual, clears selection

### P2.4 — Marks + Jump List
- [ ] T2.4.1: Create `internal/tui/marks.go`
- [ ] T2.4.2: m{a-z} sets mark at current position (view + cursor index)
- [ ] T2.4.3: '{a-z} jumps to mark (switches view and cursor)
- [ ] T2.4.4: Jump list: record position on every navigation event (view change, search jump, mark jump)
- [ ] T2.4.5: Ctrl+o back in jump list, Ctrl+i forward
- [ ] T2.4.6: `` jump to position before last jump
- [ ] T2.4.7: `:marks` overlay showing all marks

### P2.5 — Command Palette Enhancement
- [ ] T2.5.1: Command history file (~/.config/nexus/history), load on start, append on execute
- [ ] T2.5.2: Up/Down arrows cycle through history in command mode
- [ ] T2.5.3: Tab completion: cycle through matching commands and arguments
- [ ] T2.5.4: New commands: sort, filter, mark, pulse, theme, template, version, export, import, connect, favorites, recent, frequent, tags, recordings
- [ ] T2.5.5: Command aliases in config: `aliases: {c: connect, q: quit, fav: favorites}`
- [ ] T2.5.6: Argument parsing: `:sort name`, `:filter -t prod`, `:connect user@host`
- [ ] T2.5.7: Range syntax: `:1,10 delete`

### P2.6 — Undo/Redo
- [ ] T2.6.1: Create `internal/tui/undo.go` — operation stack
- [ ] T2.6.2: Operation types: ConnectionAdded, ConnectionDeleted, ConnectionEdited, ConnectionMoved, TagChanged
- [ ] T2.6.3: Record operation on every destructive action (auto, no user action needed)
- [ ] T2.6.4: u: pop undo stack, apply reverse operation, push to redo stack
- [ ] T2.6.5: Ctrl+r: pop redo stack, apply operation, push to undo stack
- [ ] T2.6.6: Flash message: "Undo: deleted 'web-server'" / "Redo: deleted 'web-server'"
- [ ] T2.6.7: Stack depth: 50

